    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1137">

                <pb facs="1029" n="715" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg715"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111W74/7</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-08-21">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 21, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 22, 6:50 a.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>446. Your August 7, 8 p.m., and my August 20, 425.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1137-f1"
                    /> Foreign Office informs me that British Government have no hesitation in
                    giving you every assurance that they will respect the neutrality of Liberia.
                    They rely on the Government of the Republic to take all proper steps to protect
                    their neutrality in any circumstances which may arise.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
